Q: Segfault using a polymorphic functor in a reference wrapper with std::views::filter A: <p>As state in comment, you have dangling reference: returning reference to local predicate.</p>
<p>If you fix that:</p>
<pre><code>Foo::FilteredView Foo::get_matches(const PredicateColor&amp; predicate)
{
  return m_table | std::views::filter(std::cref&lt;Predicate&gt;(predicate));
}

int main()
{
  // ...
  PredicateColor predicate(Color::RED);
  for (const auto&amp; item: foo.get_matches(predicate))
  // ...
}
</code></pre>
<p>It works <a href="https://godbolt.org/z/bjnPqTcb9" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<p>Another trap with for-range and temporary to avoid:</p>
<pre><code>for (const auto&amp; item: foo.get_matches(MakeTemporaryPredicate())) // Wrong before C++23
</code></pre>
<p>The lifetime of temporary predicate lifetime is not extended.</p>
